{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was a member of the House of Toulouse and played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem and succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 and was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem he was a member of the House of Toulouse and was closely related to the royal family of Jerusalem. \nHe was still a minor when his father died in 1152 and the regency was exercised by the King of Jerusalem Baldwin III. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III began his reign as Count of Tripoli in 1152 and played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states he was a member of the House of Toulouse and was closely related to the royal family of Jerusalem. \nHe was involved in several military campaigns against the Muslim states of Syria and was a key player in the politics of the Crusader states. \n*Capture and Later Life* \nRaymond III was captured by the forces of Saladin in 1164 and was imprisoned for several years he was released in 1173 and returned to Tripoli where he continued to play a significant role in the politics of the Crusader states. \nHe was a key advisor to the King of Jerusalem and played a significant role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where the Crusader states suffered a significant defeat at the hands of Saladin. \nRaymond III died in 1187 shortly after the Battle of Hattin and was succeeded as Count of Tripoli by Bohemond IV of Antioch. \n*Family and Legacy* \nRaymond III was married to Hodierna of Jerusalem and had no children he was a member of the House of Toulouse and was closely related to the royal family of Jerusalem. \nHe played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states and was a key player in the politics of the region. \nHis legacy is still remembered today and he is considered one of the most important figures of the Crusader states.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0009117737063206732}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00015948931104503572}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.8347842693328857}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.9857079386711121}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -4.291525328881107e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.008615585044026375}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -8.940656698541716e-06}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "7", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.5047034621238708}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.002870607888326049}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.08897915482521057}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.004626641049981117}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " House", "logprob": -0.0006678258068859577}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " T", "logprob": -0.004085884429514408}, {"token": "oulouse", "logprob": -0.002906386274844408}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.00032205163734033704}, {"token": " played", "logprob": -0.03658853471279144}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.014165212400257587}, {"token": " significant", "logprob": -0.002441165968775749}, {"token": " role", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " history", "l